The dummy_input() function in seq_dummy.c uses a stack variable of type `struct snd_seq_event` to store incoming events. For UMP events, which are larger than `struct snd_seq_event`, the structure assignment `tmpev = *ev` only copies the first sizeof(struct snd_seq_event) bytes, leaving the full UMP data beyond the temporary. When the dispatch path later calls `snd_seq_event_packet_size()` to determine the event size and copies that many bytes from the temporary, it reads past the end of the stack object, causing an overread.

